 "poem": "The Spirit, who kept not them alive,\nWas weeping on the dead and dying,\nAnd hid His face from all unseen.\nTo him was drawn the holiest soul,\nA flame and a glory aflame,\nTill the Earth's crown, when she afterward\nFell open unto Her, afterward\nWith that pure breath of joy arose\nThe loud and glorious cry,\nFrom a land where none have remembered,\nNo one has called of the souls unknown.\nWe did our owne doing,",
